==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|cool|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkuːl.li/|[ˈkuʷɫ.li]|/ˈkuːli/|[ˈkʉː.li]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-coolly.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hmp|en|coolie|coulee|coulis}} {{q|second pronunciation}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# At a moderately low temperature.
#: {{ux|en|The wind blew '''coolly'''.}}
# In a [[cool]], [[unpanicked]] or [[collected]] manner.
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|IV|passage="He was here," observed Drina composedly, "and father was angry with him." &para; "What?" exclaimed Eileen. "When?" &para; "This morning, before father went downtown." &para; Both Selwyn and Lansing cut in '''coolly''', dismissing the matter with a careless word or two; and coffee was served&mdash;cambric tea in Drina's case.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 2, 2011|author=Aled Williams|work=BBC Sport Wales
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/15051279.stm Swansea 2-0 Stoke]
|passage=Graham secured victory with five minutes left, '''coolly''' lifting the ball over Asmir Begovic.}}
# With calm [[impudence]].
#: {{ux|en|They walked in, not even wearing masks, and '''coolly''' robbed the bank of twelve thousand pounds.}}

